if (account.isPresent()) {
    String name = account.get().getHolderName();
    log.info("Name: {}", name);
} else {
    log.info("Not found");
}

// ✅ IDIOMATIC: functional chain
account.map(Account::getHolderName)
    .ifPresentOrElse(
        name -> log.info("Name: {}", name),
        () -> log.info("Not found")
    );
```

**Pattern 1 — map: transform if present**

```java
// map: Account → String (Optional stays wrapped)
Optional<String> name = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .map(Account::getHolderName);     // present → Optional["Rajesh"], empty → Optional.empty()

// Chained map:
String display = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .map(Account::getHolderName)       // Optional<String>
    .map(String::toUpperCase)          // Optional<String>
    .map(n -> "Welcome, " + n)         // Optional<String>
    .orElse("Welcome, Guest");         // String
```

**Pattern 2 — flatMap: avoid nested Optional**

```java
// Problem: map returns Optional<Optional<String>>!
Optional<Optional<String>> nested = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .map(Account::getMiddleName);  // getMiddleName() returns Optional<String>!
// Result: Optional<Optional<String>> — USELESS double wrapping!

// Fix: flatMap unwraps one level
Optional<String> flat = findAccount("SAV2001")
    .flatMap(Account::getMiddleName);  // flatMap: if present, call function, return its Optional directly
// Result: Optional<String> — clean!
```

**Pattern 3 — filter: conditional keep**

```java
// Only process active accounts:
findAccount("SAV2001")
    .filter(Account::isActive)          // present+active → keeps, present+dormant → empty
    .map(Account::getBalance)
    .ifPresent(bal -> log.info("Active balance: {}", bal));
```

**Pattern 4 — chaining everything together**

```java
// Complete idiomatic chain:
String result = findAccount(accountId)       // Optional<Account>
    .filter(Account::isActive)                // keep if active
    .flatMap(Account::getMiddleName)          // Optional<String> (might be absent)
    .map(String::toUpperCase)                 // transform
    .orElse("N/A");                           // default
// Zero null checks. Zero isPresent(). Zero get().
```

